From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:18:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 186/225] usb: musb: sprd: report host disconnect when leaving
 host role

An enumerated device was never torn down on unplug: it stayed in lsusb
indefinitely and the port never came free.

This board has no ID pin, so detach is signalled out of band by the TCPM
via the role switch. The controller therefore never raises a disconnect
interrupt of its own, and nothing in the teardown path told the root hub
its port had lost the connection, so usbcore kept the device alive.

Call musb_root_disconnect() when leaving host role, guarded on the port
actually being enabled, as the sunxi glue does for the same reason. It
sets the C_CONNECTION change bit and kicks usb_hcd_poll_rh_status(), which
is what makes usbcore unbind the device.

Take musb->lock across it: every other caller runs from the interrupt
handler with the lock held, whereas the role switch does not.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/usb/musb/sprd.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/musb/sprd.c b/drivers/usb/musb/sprd.c
index 1a97f53f7..d551c21c9 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/musb/sprd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/musb/sprd.c
@@ -29,6 +29,7 @@ struct sprd_glue {
 static int sprd_otg_switch_set(struct sprd_glue *glue, enum usb_role role)
 {
 	struct musb *musb = glue->musb;
+	unsigned long flags;
 	u8 devctl;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -38,6 +39,20 @@ static int sprd_otg_switch_set(struct sprd_glue *glue, enum usb_role role)
 	devctl = musb_readb(musb->mregs, MUSB_DEVCTL);
 
 	if (glue->role != USB_ROLE_NONE) {
+		/*
+		 * Leaving host role: tell the root hub the port lost its
+		 * connection. Detach is signalled out of band by the TCPM (no ID
+		 * pin on this board), so the controller never raises a disconnect
+		 * interrupt of its own and usbcore would otherwise keep the
+		 * enumerated device around forever.
+		 */
+		if (glue->role == USB_ROLE_HOST) {
+			spin_lock_irqsave(&musb->lock, flags);
+			if (musb->port1_status & USB_PORT_STAT_ENABLE)
+				musb_root_disconnect(musb);
+			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&musb->lock, flags);
+		}
+
 		/* force disconnect */
 		musb->is_active = 0;
 		devctl &= ~MUSB_DEVCTL_SESSION;
